          "normalized_title": "Breakthrough Parkinson’s Drug Targets Disease at Its Genetic Roots",
          "normalized_summary": "An experimental gene-silencing therapy safely lowered LRRK2 protein levels in an early Parkinson’s trial, but its effect on symptoms remains untested. An experimental medicine built to silence a gene closely associated with Parkinson’s disease has produced encouraging results in its first clinical test in people, according to a study published in Nature Medicine. The treatment, [...]",
